  "paradigm_pack_notes": "Gilgamesh is a high-end Commando with quick-hitting attacks and spells; he casts spells faster than Serah and his physical attacks are also swift. Gilgamesh has high Strength and Magic and he can gain a massive amount of HP. All of his stats can be even further raised through infusions. With the right build, it is possible to have a Gilgamesh with 14,000+ HP and over 1,200+ Strength.\n\nGilgamesh's uses his different swords for his Attack command, each with its own effect: Excalipoor deals only 1 point of damage; Excalibur deals double damage; Muramasa is used as the last attack of the ATB gauge and recovers HP equal to 10% of the damage dealt; Bashosen is used for Powerchain and Blindside, and deals wind-elemental magical damage; Zantetsuken is used for Scourge and deals 10% wound damage. Armor Breaker and Stagger: Wound override all sword effects. Against aerial targets, Gilgamesh uses Death Claw which deals 10% wound damage and stacks with Stagger: Wound for a total of 20% wound damage. He uses Cross Slash for Ravage.\n\nDue to Excalipoor, Gilgamesh's AI tends to favor using Ruin over Attack, despite him having higher Strength than Magic.\n\nGilgamesh's Feral Link, Divider, is a timing attack that hits three times; pressing / at the right time strengthens these attacks.",
